        <head>Wycliffe P.S.A. Society.</head>
        <p>Wycliffe P.S.A. Society.</p>
        <p>The meeting of this society on Sunday waa presided over by Mr H Farrar. There was an average attend- ance of about 500 men. An xcellent address was de-- livered by Mr Fenn, of Liverpotl. His subject was " Colour-blindness." Mr William Beswic4 reterred to the fact that the president of the society completed his 25th year of service that day and suggested that the secretaiy should write to the Rev John Yonge on their behalf, congratulating him upon the interesting event- This course was adopted. Mr A Griffiths sang a is( 1,3 from Mendelssohn's " Hymn of Praise " and ale) 6, The Promise° Land." The meeting was also taken part 10 by Mr Downes and Mr Maley.</p>
