        <p>Mr F. Monks and the New Police Court. On taking his seat at the Borough Police Court on Monday, Mr F Monks, the presiding magistrate, asked the Clerk when it was intended to warm the building. Mr White explained that the heating apparatus had been tried but had broken down, and this bnaught forth the remark from Mr Monks : " It. is a sluice that we should be brought here to Sit In a cold room like this. I caught a cold here said : last MonclAy "—Later on Mr Monks speaking to a press representative, in alluding t 3 the building generally "It is a sheer waste,of money altogether."</p>
