      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1901-11-01_WidnesExaminer_art0108" n="art0108">
        <head>HOCKEY</head>
        <p>HOCKEY</p>
        <p>STOCKTON EIEATH V. KERSAL.</p>
        <p>Played at Stockton Heath on Saturday in lovely weather. Play was of a very even character for the first quarter of an hour, both sides attacking in turn. Stockton Heath scored the first goal by means of Sandy, and continue ll pressing until half-time. On changing over Kersal evidently meant business and pressed hard, being at length rewarded by a goad goal, making the score 1 nil. Shortly afterwards Stockton Heath scored again out of a tcrimmsge in the goal mouth from the stick of Houghton Owen andifollowed it up immediately afterwards with a third goal from a good shot by Sandy Kersal's combination seemed now to be broken up, their forwards all converging on the centre. When the whistle was blown the score was Stockton Heath three 20AI°, Kenai one. For the winners, L Fairelcugh and E E Woods played an exceptionally fine game. LATCHFORD 2ND V. ASHLEY.</p>
        <p>This match wre pLryed at Latchtord on Saturday and a very even game resulted in a win for the home club by two goals t 3 nit.</p>
