      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1901-11-01_WidnesExaminer_art0126" n="art0126">
        <head>Church of the Sacred Heart.</head>
        <p>Church of the Sacred Heart.</p>
        <p>On Sunday the annual sermons in aid of the above church were preached by the liPv. Father Davidson, C.S.S.R., whose discourses were listened to with deep ittere:t by large congregations. The music selected for the morning service was Mozart's &amp;vent% Mass. "0 Salutaris" was sung at the offertory by Mr. Hubert Bowen, tenor, in an admirable manner. At the I evening service there was a rosary sermon, and Berle- ' (Fenno. After the sermon "0 Sacrum" was rendered in a very eretitable manner by the following: Miss A. Fairclough (treble), Mr G. No wton (tenor). and Mr J. Gibbins (bass). The singing of the eh.oir reflected great credit upon their conductor, Mr J. Gibbine. Miss M. Hellian presided at the organ.</p>
